  "axis_lesson": "One shared linear Aging Temperature (F) X and four independent linear Ys: Ftu (upper left), Fty (upper right), RA (lower left), and e(1 in) (lower right). At the same height, left Ftu=170 corresponds to right Fty=180, and left RA=0 corresponds to right e=10. These same-unit pairs have different origins and must stay separate. In contrast, RA/e can share one Y in other figures when their printed mappings coincide; decide from this image's ticks, not the property names. Error bars and curves do not change the Axis structure."
